      "headers": [
        "Aristotelian Argument",
        "Why It Seemed Compelling"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Nature abhors a vacuum: two objects in contact can't be pulled apart without creating void, yet they can be pulled apart, therefore no void",
          "Empirically, surfaces seem to resist separation"
        ],
        [
          "How do atoms explain qualities like hot/cold without invoking qualities?",
          "Circularity: \"round atoms explain fire\" just names the association"
        ],
        [
          "No teleology: atoms can't explain purposive processes like growth, development",
          "Biological development seems goal-directed"
        ],
        [
          "Infinite divisibility of continuum: mathematical continuum requires infinite divisibility",
          "Mathematical argument seemed stronger"
        ]
      ]
